{"r":"xTw","lane":{"p":768,"e":[{"h":"خَطَا","t":["(S, Msb, K, &c.,) aor. ",[2,"يَخْطُو"],", (Msb,) inf. n. ",[2,"خَطْوٌ"],"; (Msb, K;) and ↓ ",[2,"اختطى"],"; (S, K;) said of a man (S, Msb, TA) [and of a beast]; both signify the same; (S, K;) ",[1,"He stepped, paced,"]," or ",[1,"walked;"]," (MA, KL;) ",[1,"i. q."],[2,"مَشَى"],"; (M, Msb, K;) as also ",[2,"اِخْتَاطَ"],", [which see in art. ",[2,"خيط"],",] formed by transposition. (K.) You say, ",[2,"خَطَوْتُ"],[2,"خَطْوَةً وَاحِدَةً"]," [",[1,"I stepped one step"],"]. (JK.) [And ",[2,"وَسَّعَ الخَطْوَ"],[1,"He stepped wide."],"] See also the last sentence of the next paragraph."],"f":"1"},{"h":"خطّى","t":[[1,"He made to pass over:"]," so in the saying, ",[2,"خَطَّى ٱللّٰهُ نَوْءَهَا"],[1,"God made,"]," or ",[1,"may God make, its"]," (a land's) [",[1,"rain-giving"],"] ",[1,"star"]," or ",[1,"asterism to pass it over, and not send rain upon it:"]," (TA in art. ",[2,"خطأ"],":) but in this case the verb is, (Mgh in that art.,) or may be, (TA ibid.,) originally ",[2,"خَطَّطَ"],", the final ",[2,"ط"]," being changed into ",[2,"ى"],". (Mgh and TA ibid. [See 2 in art. ",[2,"خطأ"],".]) Accord. to Fr, ",[2,"خَطَّى السَّهْمَ"]," and ",[2,"خطأ"]," are syn. [as meaning ",[1,"He made the arrow to pass over,"]," or ",[1,"to miss,"]," the mark]. (TA in art. ",[2,"خطأ"],".) One says also, in praying for a man, ",[2,"خُطِّىَ عَنْهُ السُّوْءُ"]," [",[1,"May evil be made to pass him;"]," or] ",[1,"may evil be repelled from him:"]," and one says also ",[2,"خُطِّىَ عَنْكَ"],[1,"May it be removed,"]," or ",[1,"put away, from thee:"]," (S, TA:) or ",[2,"خُطِّئَ عَنْكَ السُّوْءُ"],". (ISk, TA in art. ",[2,"خطأ"],".) -A2- The vulgar say [to a she-ass and to a she-camel or other beast in a slippery or difficult place] ",[2,"خَطِّى"],", meaning ",[2,"اِمْشِى"]," [for ",[2,"اِمْشِى رُوَيَدًا"],[1,"Step thou leisurely"],"]: but the correct word is ↓ ",[2,"اُخْطُِى"]," [imperative fem. of ",[2,"خَطَا"],"]. (TA.)"],"f":"2"},{"h":"اخطاهُ","t":[[1,"He"]," (a man) ",[1,"made him"]," (another man) ",[1,"to step, pace,"]," or ",[1,"walk."]," (S, TA.) -A2- ",[2,"أَخْطَيْتُ"]," for ",[2,"أَخْطَأْتُ"],": see the latter."],"f":"4"},{"h":"تَخَطَّيْتُهُ","t":[[1,"I stepped,"]," or ",[1,"walked, over him,"]," or ",[1,"it:"]," (Msb:) or ",[1,"I passed over and beyond him,"]," or ",[1,"it:"]," (S:) or ",[2,"تخطّى النَّاسَ"],[1,"He went over the people,"]," (",[2,"رَكِبَهُمْ"],",) ",[1,"and passed beyond them;"]," and so ↓ ",[2,"اِخْتَطَاهُمْ"],". (K.) One says, ",[2,"تَخَطَّيْتُ رِقَابَ النَّاسِ"]," [",[1,"I stepped over, walked over, passed over and beyond,"]," or ",[1,"went over and passed beyond, the necks of the people"],"]. (S, TA.) It is said in a trad. respecting Friday, [of one who came too late to the Friday-prayers, as is shown in the TA in art. ",[2,"انى"],",] ",[2,"رَأَى رَجُلًا يَتَخَطَّى رِقَابَ النَّاسِ"],[1,"He saw a man passing step by step"]," [",[1,"over the necks of the people"]," who were already in their ranks in the mosque]. (TA. [See also Har p. 83.]) One says also, ",[2,"فُلَانٌ لَا"],[2,"يَتَخَطَّى عَنِ الطُّنُبِ"]," [",[1,"Such a one will not step over,"]," or ",[1,"beyond,"]," or ",[1,"from, the tent-rope"],"], meaning, ",[1,"will not go far from the tent for the purpose of voiding his excrement,"]," by reason of his foulness and vileness and uncleanness. (TA.) And ",[2,"تَخَطَّيْتُ"],[2,"كَذَا"]," (S, TA) ",[1,"I passed over"]," [",[1,"to such a thing"]," or ",[1,"place"]," or ",[1,"person"],"]: (TA:) one should not say ",[2,"تَخَطَّأْتُ"]," [in this sense], with ",[2,"ء"],". (S, TA.) [Hence the following tropical phrases.] ",[2,"تخطّاهُ المَكْرُوهُ"]," (tropical:) [",[1,"What was disliked"]," or ",[1,"hated,"]," or ",[1,"evil, passed over him;"]," not alighting upon him]. (TA.) And ",[2,"تَخَطَّيْتُ إِلَيْهِ بِالمَكْرُوهِ"]," (tropical:) [",[1,"I passed over"]," others ",[1,"to him with that which was disliked"]," or ",[1,"hated,"]," or ",[1,"evil; i. q."],[2,"تَجَاوَزْتُ"],"]. (TA.) And ",[2,"تخطّى عَنِّى"],[2,"بَصَرُكَ"]," (assumed tropical:) [",[1,"Thine eye,"]," or ",[1,"thy sight, passed me over"],"]. (Aboo-Turáb, TA in art. ",[2,"تيه"],".) ― -b2- [Also (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"I overstepped it,"]," or ",[1,"transgressed it;"]," namely, a limit prescribed to me, &c.]"],"f":"5"},{"h":"إِخْتَطَوَ","t":["see 1: -A2- and see also 5."],"f":"8"},{"h":"خَطْوَةٌ","t":[[1,"A step,"]," or ",[1,"pace,"]," as meaning a ",[1,"single act of stepping"]," or ",[1,"pacing"]," or ",[1,"walking:"]," (JK, S, K, Msb:) pl. [of pauc.] ",[2,"خَطَوَاتٌ"]," (S, Msb, K) and [of mult.] ",[2,"خِطَآءٌ"],". (S.) Imra-el-Keys says, ",[2,"لَهَا وَثَبَاتٌ كَوَثْبِ الشِّبَآءِ"],[2,"فَوَادٍ خِطَآءٌ وَوَادٍ مَطِرْ"]," [",[1,"She has bounds like the bounding of gazelles; and a valley is"]," stepped over by her with leisurely ",[1,"steps, and a valley is"]," trampled over by her rapidly as though it were ",[1,"rained upon"],"]: (S:) i. e., one time she steps, and refrains from running; and one time she runs with a running resembling rain: but AO relates it otherwise, saying, ",[2,"فَوَادٍ"],[2,"خَطِيطٌ"]," [lit. ",[1,"and a valley is not rained upon"],"]: and some substitute ",[2,"كَصَوْبِ الخَرِيفِ"]," [",[1,"like the pouring rain of the autumn"],"]. (IB, TA.) [See also what next follows.]"]},{"h":"خُطْوَةٌ","t":[[1,"A step,"]," or ",[1,"pace,"]," as meaning the ",[1,"space between the two feet"]," [",[1,"in walking"]," or ",[1,"running"],"]: pl. (of pauc., S) ",[2,"خُطْوَاتٌ"]," (S, Msb, K) and ",[2,"خُطُوَاتٌ"]," and ",[2,"خُطَوَاتٌ"]," (S, Msb) and (of mult., S) ",[2,"خُطًى"],". (S, Msb, K.) One says, ",[2,"قَرَّبَ ٱللّٰهُ عَلَيْكَ الخُطْوَةَ"],", meaning ",[1,"May God make short to thee the space,"]," or ",[1,"distance."]," (TA.) And ",[2,"بَيْنَ القَوْلَيْنِ خُطٍى يَسِيرَةٌ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"Between the two sayings is little difference."]," (TA.) ",[2,"لَا تَتَّبِعُوا خُطُوَاتِ الشَّيْطَانِ"],", in the Kur [ii. 163 &c.], means [",[1,"Follow not ye"],"] ",[1,"the ways of the Devil:"]," (TA:) or ",[1,"the footsteps of the Devil:"]," (JK:) here some read ",[2,"خُطْوَات"],"; and some, accord. to Lth, ",[2,"خُطُؤَات"],", which Az pronounces to have no meaning. (TA.)"]},{"h":"خَطِيَّةٌ","t":["for ",[2,"خَطِيْئَةٌ"],": see the latter, in art. ",[2,"خطأ"],". [Freytag, evidently from his having found it incorrectly written for ",[2,"حَظِيَّةٌ"],", has assigned to it the meaning of “ amica, ” and “ amata. ”]"]},{"h":"نَاقَتُكَ هٰذِهِ مِنَ المُتَخَطِّيَاتِ الجيف","t":["[the last word being app. ",[2,"الجِيَفَ"],"] is a saying mentioned by AZ: (TA in the present art.:) or ",[2,"من"],[2,"المُتَخَطِّئَاتِ الجيف"],". (TA in art. ",[2,"خطأ"],", where see the explanation.)"]}]},"mufradat":["خطوت أخطو خطوة، أي: مرة، والخطوة ما بين القدمين ، قال تعالى: ولا تتبعوا خطوات الشيطان [البقرة/ 168] ، أي: لا تتبعوه، وذلك نحو قوله: ولا تتبع الهوى [ص/ 26] ."]}